# E2E Testing Rules (StyleUp)

## Feature gate

Any feature implementation where e2e is relevant → create or update the e2e test case also (`test/*.e2e-spec.ts`). Do not ship HTTP/integration behavior covered only by unit mocks when e2e applies.

## When e2e is required

- New or changed public HTTP endpoints / API contracts
- Auth, payment, or booking flows (session, OTP, pay, slot booking)
- Migration-backed DB constraints that protect concurrency or integrity (EXCLUDE, uniqueness)
- Multi-adapter wiring that unit port mocks cannot prove

## When e2e is not required

- Pure refactors with no behavior change
- Internal helpers fully covered by unit tests
- Scaffolding-only / setup tasks with no feature logic

## Skip policy

- Do not add new `describe.skip` / `it.skip` for unfinished e2e without explicit user approval.
- Existing skips must keep a `TODO` comment stating why and when to re-enable.

## Authoring baseline

- Bootstrap with `test/helpers/create-test-app.ts`; close the app in `afterAll`.
- Assert the mobile API envelope (`success`, `data`, `error.code`, `error.message`).
- Prefer `truncatePostgres` / `clearRedis` over ad-hoc cleanup.

Pitfalls and local-stack failure triage → see the **e2e-testing** skill (do not duplicate here).

When changing “when to write e2e,” update this rule’s lists and the skill decision table together.
